IMPORT prelude

-- Industrial Relations Act 2016 (Qld) -- small helpers for dates and amounts, used by qira-claims.l4 and
-- qira-seat.l4. Built on the stable prelude's date primitives (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL,
-- DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR); the daydate library is not imported.
--
-- READINGS (the Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld) is not deposited):
-- * "within 21 days after" a day ends 21 days after it: the day itself is excluded and the 21st day is the last day.
-- * "within 6 years after" or "within 6 months after" a day ends on the same day and month 6 years (or months) later.
-- * A period of months or years that starts on a day the end month does not have (31 August, 29 February) ends on
--   the last day of the end month (31 August + 6 months = 28 or 29 February).
-- * "the first 3 months of employment" are the days before the day 3 months after employment started.
-- * Service is "more than n years" on a day after the n-th anniversary of its start, and "at least n years" on the
--   anniversary or after.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates and amounts`

GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
      `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` `x` `and` `y` MEANS
    IF `x` AT MOST `y` THEN `x` ELSE `y`

GIVEN `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a leap year` `y` IF
        (`y` MODULO 4 EQUALS 0 AND (NOT (`y` MODULO 100 EQUALS 0)))
    OR  `y` MODULO 400 EQUALS 0

GIVEN `m` IS A NUMBER
      `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days in month` `m` `of` `y` MEANS
    IF `m` EQUALS 2
    THEN IF `is a leap year` `y` THEN 29 ELSE 28
    ELSE IF `m` EQUALS 4 OR `m` EQUALS 6 OR `m` EQUALS 9 OR `m` EQUALS 11
         THEN 30
         ELSE 31

-- The same day n months later, or the last day of that month where it is shorter.
GIVEN `n`         IS A NUMBER
      `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day that is` `n` `months after` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (`the lesser of` (DATE_DAY `the start`) `and` (`the number of days in month` `month` `of` `year`)) `month` `year`
    WHERE
        `months since year 0` MEANS ((DATE_YEAR `the start`) TIMES 12) PLUS ((DATE_MONTH `the start`) MINUS 1) PLUS `n`
        `year`  MEANS TRUNC (`months since year 0` DIVIDED BY 12) 0
        `month` MEANS `months since year 0` MINUS (`year` TIMES 12) PLUS 1

GIVEN `n`         IS A NUMBER
      `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day that is` `n` `years after` `the start` MEANS `the day that is` (`n` TIMES 12) `months after` `the start`

GIVEN `n`         IS A NUMBER
      `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day that is` `n` `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL ((DATE_SERIAL `the start`) PLUS `n`)

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE
      `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a` `is on or before` `b` IF DATE_SERIAL `a` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE
      `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a` `is before` `b` IF DATE_SERIAL `a` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE
      `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days from` `a` `to` `b` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `b` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `a`

-- Service that started on `start` is more than n years long on `the day`.
GIVEN `start`   IS A DATE
      `n`       IS A NUMBER
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `service from` `start` `is more than` `n` `years on` `the day` IF
    (`the day that is` `n` `years after` `start`) `is before` `the day`

-- Service that started on `start` is at least n years long on `the day`.
GIVEN `start`   IS A DATE
      `n`       IS A NUMBER
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `service from` `start` `is at least` `n` `years on` `the day` IF
    (`the day that is` `n` `years after` `start`) `is on or before` `the day`

-- A person born on `birth` is n or older on `the day` (a 29 February birthday falls on 28 February in other years).
GIVEN `birth`   IS A DATE
      `n`       IS A NUMBER
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `someone born on` `birth` `is at least` `n` `on` `the day` IF
    (`the day that is` `n` `years after` `birth`) `is on or before` `the day`
